    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured audit event in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`. Alongside the existing audit *line*, each successful owner create now emits an immutable JSON event on the dedicated `AUDIT` logger:\n\n```json\n{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nKey points of the change:\n\n- **`seq` \u2014 monotonic across creates:** a `static final AtomicLong OWNER_CREATED_SEQUENCE`, incremented once per create, gives every event a strictly increasing global sequence number.\n- **Current primary identifier:** the `customerCode` field is populated from `primaryIdentifier(owner)` (not `owner.getCustomerCode()` directly). That accessor already exists as the single abstraction point for the owner's primary identifier \u2014 so when the customer code is later unified into the member id, updating only `primaryIdentifier` makes this event automatically carry the member id, exactly as the spec requires.\n- **Immutable structured event:** modeled as a private `record OwnerCreatedEvent(...)` serialized with Jackson (`tools.jackson`, the version already used in this repo), so the event is a value object rather than an inline string.\n- **Placement:** emission lives in a new `auditOwnerCreatedEvent` helper called from the existing `auditOwnerCreated` \u2014 matching the class's documented convention that further create-time audit side-effects are added as sibling helpers rather than inline in the pipeline.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest` passes and the full build is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
